# Docs (generators) — ai-project-docs

Rule exclusive to this repo. Read `src/docs/README.md`. All generated Markdown must be **English**.

## Flow

```
DocumentationPlan + ProjectKnowledge
  → TemplateEngine (src/templates/)
  → Rendered content
  → documentation-writer.ts
  → .ai-docs/*.md
```

## Four separate concerns

1. **Planning** — `documentation-planner.ts` → `DocumentationPlan`
2. **Rendering** — `markdown-renderers/` (PKM → Markdown)
3. **Templating** — `src/templates/markdown-template.ts` (dispatch)
4. **Writing** — `documentation-writer.ts` (disk I/O + marker policy)

## New Markdown document

1. Renderer in `markdown-renderers/<name>-renderer.ts` — `ProjectKnowledge` only
2. Register `TemplateDefinition` in `src/templates/markdown-template.ts`
3. Add to planner if needed (`documentation-planner.ts`)
4. Tests in `src/templates/template-engine.test.ts`

Unregistered documents fall back to generic template in `document-template.ts`.

## Incremental regeneration

When `analysis.documentImpact` exists, rewrite only impacted docs. Files without `<!-- Generated by AI Project Docs. Safe to update. -->` are **preserved**.

## Existing renderers

`architecture`, `folder-structure`, `dependency-map`, `conventions`, `agent-navigation`, `ai-context`, `implementation-guide` — see README table.

## Hard stops

- Repo scan or config parsing inside renderers
- OpenRouter in renderers
- Write PKM JSON — that is `src/knowledge/knowledge-writer.ts`
- Hardcode facts — read from PKM
- Delete files from docs dir
- Non-English generated Markdown
